# Round 64: the `prev of` undefined-name guard was scoped to MODULE level
# only -- the per-scope-guard class, tenth sighting. `prev of p` inside a
# function, p bound NOWHERE, answered null rc 0 where the VM raises
# "undefined variable 'p'" rc 1: silent-wrong via a plain typo. The guard
# now has a function-scope half keyed on the never-bound set (g_cur_bound:
# params + body assigns + locals + for-binders, conservative-inclusive,
# unioned with g_module_names) -- statically decidable, and it also covers
# names bound only in OTHER functions' bodies (never in scope here).
# Both sides die "undefined variable 'p'", equal codes (_err class).
define a() as:
    print of (prev of p)
    return 0
a of []
print of "done"
